Subject: TDEUniqueApplication -- defer to a running instance on the nofork path

Companion to patch 0005 (force KUniqueApplication s_nofork=true).  The fork()
launch path detects an already-running instance and hands the request to it via
newInstance() before exiting; the nofork path did not -- it just called
registerAs(appName, false), which for a taken name returns "<name>-2" and runs a
duplicate.  Since patch 0005 forces every TDEUniqueApplication down the nofork
path, any unique app launched twice (e.g. the ksmserver desktop launch AND the
DCOP autostart both starting kdesktop/kicker) produced duplicate panels/desktops.

Mirror the fork parent on the nofork path: if the app is already registered, hand
the request to the running instance via newInstance() and exit with its return
code, instead of registering a duplicate.

--- a/tdecore/kuniqueapplication.cpp
+++ b/tdecore/kuniqueapplication.cpp
@@ -123,6 +123,43 @@
         appName = appName + "-" + pid;
      }
 
+#ifndef TQ_WS_WIN
+     /* substrate: defer to an already-running instance instead of registering a
+      * duplicate "<name>-2".  Patch 0005 forces this nofork path for every
+      * TDEUniqueApplication, but — unlike the fork path below — it never checked
+      * whether the app was already running, so any unique app launched twice
+      * (e.g. the ksmserver workaround AND the autostart both starting
+      * kdesktop/kicker) produced duplicate panels/desktops.  Mirror the fork
+      * parent: hand the request to the running instance via newInstance() and
+      * exit with its return code. */
+     if (!s_multipleInstances && dcopClient()->isApplicationRegistered(appName))
+     {
+        TQByteArray data, reply;
+        TQDataStream ds(data, IO_WriteOnly);
+        TDECmdLineArgs::saveAppArgs(ds);
+        TQCString new_asn_id;
+#if defined TQ_WS_X11
+        TDEStartupInfoId id = TDEStartupInfo::currentStartupIdEnv();
+        if (!id.none())
+           new_asn_id = id.id();
+#endif
+        ds << new_asn_id;
+        dcopClient()->setPriorityCall(true);
+        TQCString replyType;
+        if (dcopClient()->call(appName, TDECmdLineArgs::about->appName(),
+                               "newInstance()", data, replyType, reply)
+            && (replyType == "int"))
+        {
+           TQDataStream rs(reply, IO_ReadOnly);
+           int exitCode = 0;
+           rs >> exitCode;
+           ::exit(exitCode);
+        }
+        dcopClient()->setPriorityCall(false);
+        /* newInstance failed -> fall through and register (best effort) */
+     }
+#endif
+
      // Check to make sure that we're actually able to register with the DCOP
      // server.
 
